  "finding": "Every in-session failure was reproduced, but every accepted state picture failed: question 4 asks each observer for a worried patient's misreading, and the coder mapped single imagined misreadings onto forbidden readings (an eye patch as the ear uncovered, an ordinary hearing aid as a hearing aid with no coil, a fresh incision as an open wound), and the swelling image failed on the negative item \"no liquid on the surface\", which no observer states. Re-scoring the recorded codings offline: the current rule agrees 7 of 11; failing only when two observers share a harmful misreading agrees 6 of 11; treating misreadings as notes for the clinician agrees 9 of 11. The image cases were not run, because a gate that fails every accepted picture passes the negative controls trivially."
